<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Negara Daha</h1><p class="st-meta">1495 CE – 1526 CE (approx.) · capital Negara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Hindu kingdom of South Kalimantan, whose succession dispute gave rise to the Banjar Sultanate in 1526.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hikayat-banjar">Hikayat Banjar</a>, the royal seat of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/negara-dipa">Negara Dipa</a> was moved downriver to a place called Negara, on the Negara River, and the kingdom became known as Negara Daha. The details come only from this later chronicle, and the dates are approximate.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Negara Daha controlled trade on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barito-river">Barito</a> river system, and its rulers looked to Javanese models of kingship. Its port at Muara Bahan traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. The chronicle names <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja-sukarama">Maharaja Sukarama</a> as king.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja-sukarama">Sukarama</a>'s death his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pangeran-tumenggung">Pangeran Tumenggung</a> seized the throne, and the king's grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-suriansyah">Raden Samudra</a> fled to the coast. With military help from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/demak-sultanate">Demak</a>, Raden Samudra won the war, accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Suriansyah, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banjar-sultanate">Banjar Sultanate</a> in 1526. Pangeran Tumenggung submitted, and Negara Daha came to an end.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1495 CE – 1526 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Maritime Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.45%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1495 CE – 1526 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Negara</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Maharaja Sukarama, Pangeran Tumenggung</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Banjar Malay</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nagara Daha</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1510&amp;focus=negara-daha" aria-label="Negara Daha on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7848 2490 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Negara Daha lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8168 2746L8200 2524M8168 2746L8181 2558"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8200 2524h0M8181 2558h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8168 2746h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8168 2746h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Negara. <a href="/atlas?year=1510&amp;focus=negara-daha">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
